WEBVTT

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.860
I won't go.

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:27.450
We should be looking for Yuya, not some 
duelist we don't even know.

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:29.980
H-Hang on, Gonny.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.070
It's possible that Yuya could be here, too.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:35.110
Yuya? Here?

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.020
The Lancers' goal is to find strong duelists here,

00:00:39.020 --> 00:00:42.090
in the Synchro Dimension, and get 
them to join us, right?

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:45.700
So Yuya might have heard the 
rumors and come here. Right?

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.440
But are there really strong duelists here?

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.080
Are there?

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:56.140
I am the sharp-eyed promoter, Gallagher.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:59.070
You think I'd lie about something like this?

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:00.710
Let's go!

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.060
H-Hey!

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.540
D-Wheels.

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.810
Riding duels are fought while 
racing on these machines,

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:14.460
which are an evolution of the duel disks.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:17.870
They combine speed and thrills for the ultimate show,

00:01:17.870 --> 00:01:20.040
a symbol of freedom to all.

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:58.790
Invitation to the Dark Duels

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:11.970
Here, we are! You can see for 
yourselves if it's the real thing!

00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:20.210
Wh-What is this place?

00:03:20.640 --> 00:03:23.650
This is City's biggest underground duel venue.

00:03:23.650 --> 00:03:27.840
An underworld meeting spot that 
engages in illegal duel betting.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.180
Duel betting?

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.020
You want us to stay in such an ignoble place...

00:03:32.180 --> 00:03:32.960
What?

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:35.850
Kurosaki!

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:37.900
Xyz Summon!

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:44.340
Appear, Rank 4 Raidraptor — Rise Falcon!

00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.880
I was wondering what the famous 
Xyz Summon would have to offer.

00:03:52.270 --> 00:03:54.940
So it's just a 100-attack-point monster?

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.060
The effect of Rise Falcon.

00:03:58.060 --> 00:04:01.630
I use one Overlay Unit to add the attack points

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:06.640
of all monsters Special Summoned 
to your side of the field, to its own!

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.530
What?!

00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:09.940
Battle.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:13.330
Raidraptor — Rise Falcon, tear through everything!

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:16.530
Flame Claw Evolution!

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:29.280
Kurosaki! Kurosaki! Kurosaki!

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:34.780
Why? To find strong duelists, obviously.

00:04:34.780 --> 00:04:37.260
See? I told you we'd find

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:40.960
more strong duelists in a shady place 
like this than up in town!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.530
Because I heard

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:48.430
that true, fair tests of strength happened 
in this underground duel venue.

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.930
But it's boring.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:55.410
They're all talk. I haven't met a 
single one worth fighting!

00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:01.440
He's taken nine straight wins, with his shocking

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.380
Xyz Summoning technique.

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.580
It's no shock to me, of course...

00:05:06.850 --> 00:05:11.550
I can see that. So you were together, were you?

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:12.560
I suppose it stands to reason.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:18.030
The Xyz you learn at LDS is nothing but an imitation.

00:05:18.030 --> 00:05:19.960
Oh, really?

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.740
But your Xyz Monsters aren't actually 
all that strong, are they?

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:25.790
What did you say?

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:27.210
Stop fighting!

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:31.910
Kurosaki, where are Yuya and the others?

00:05:32.230 --> 00:05:35.850
I don't know. I arrived in this dimension,

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:37.560
and came this far by myself.

00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:41.890
I thought the rest might have been lost 
in the gap between dimensions.

00:05:41.890 --> 00:05:43.530
You haven't even looked for them?!

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:45.830
I'm looking for strong duelists.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:48.440
That's the reason we came here, after all.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:52.100
Our priority should be searching 
for our fellow Lancers!

00:05:52.380 --> 00:05:53.530
Lancers?

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:57.070
What's that? And you've been talking 
about dimensions or something?

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.780
The truth is, we've come to the Synchro 
Dimension from the Standard—

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:03.930
What are you doing?

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:07.870
Now, now. We can discuss 
the complicated stuff later!

00:06:07.870 --> 00:06:09.610
What was that?

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.550
Explaining about other dimensions 
will take more time than it's worth.

00:06:12.550 --> 00:06:14.520
Hey, you! What are you whispering about?

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:20.990
Hey, so you reached out to us because 
Kurosaki is too strong, didn't you?

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.560
That's right.

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:26.740
I was looking for unaffiliated new 
players, and I found you.

00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:28.430
Especially you, Dennis!

00:06:28.830 --> 00:06:31.580
You have what it takes to be a star!

00:06:31.580 --> 00:06:35.810
I've been doing this a long time, 
and I don't make mistakes!

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:40.440
I'm so flattered to have you say 
that to me, Mr. Gallagher!

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:42.030
Dennis, are you seriously...

00:06:42.030 --> 00:06:44.560
Yeah, I think I might give it a try.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.050
Gambling duels? Outrageous!

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:49.720
But the duels here certainly are strange.

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.000
You ride those motorcycle things...

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:56.390
D-Wheels. What, you've never 
seen a riding duel before?

00:06:56.770 --> 00:06:58.630
A riding duel?

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:04.840
Riding duels started as a game 
we Commons played.

00:07:05.140 --> 00:07:06.070
A game?

00:07:06.070 --> 00:07:08.010
Crow told us so.

00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:12.110
Street punks used to ride, dueling, 
through the city.

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:12.750
Right?

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:15.790
Yeah, then guys started using highways

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:20.420
and driving through City, acting like 
they owned the place!

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:26.420
Even the Tops that looked down 
on us were amazed by them.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:30.660
Dueling at high speeds? Sounds exhilarating...

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:34.280
Riding duels were a symbol of freedom.

00:07:34.280 --> 00:07:36.370
So they became a huge fad immediately.

00:07:36.370 --> 00:07:41.110
I mean, all of the Commons are always 
itching to show up the Tops.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:47.300
Hey, why don't you go over there 
and join in the conversation?

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:55.290
Damn. How long do we have to stay here?

00:07:57.190 --> 00:07:59.760
But the Tops didn't stay quiet.

00:08:00.150 --> 00:08:04.920
They said riding duels disrupted City's 
peace, and sent security after us.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.570
And they formed a specialist squad 
called the Duel Chasers.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.420
Duel Chasers?

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.740
Security that ride on D-Wheels.

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.340
If you lose the duel...

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:17.680
You're arrested on the spot, 
and taken straight to prison!

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:19.760
Without even a trial?

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.410
Those security guys are cruel.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:23.880
That time...

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:30.810
If Crow hadn't come, we also 
would have probably...

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:33.420
It isn't just security that's cruel!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:35.620
Crow!

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:39.800
The Tops stole riding duels from us!

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:41.320
Stole?

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:44.350
Then none of the Commons do it anymore?

00:08:44.350 --> 00:08:49.080
We're forced to do it. As a show for the Tops.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:50.010
A show?

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:52.480
When a highway chase starts,

00:08:52.480 --> 00:08:57.250
the streets become duel-only highways, 
and TV cameras come and start filming.

00:08:57.610 --> 00:09:01.850
The riding duels that we started to 
thumb our noses at the Tops

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.960
now exist to amuse them.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:11.480
Yuya, if you go out there now, you'll be 
chased by security and filmed, too.

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:13.910
If you don't want to be humiliated, 
stay where you are.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:15.430
You, too.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:22.410
So the city's full of security, and we're 
supposed to tuck tail and run?

00:09:22.690 --> 00:09:23.840
What was that?

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:24.410
Hey!

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:26.810
Don't we have any information on Yuzu?

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:30.140
Serena, Crow's working hard to help...

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:32.920
Hard work is meaningless 
if it doesn't produce results!

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.390
H-Hey, where are you going?

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:40.860
Where else? I'm going to search 
for information myself.

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:43.810
If you want to get caught, then go ahead!

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.650
Maybe I'll go, too...

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:50.280
I can't breathe, just sticking 
around here all the time.

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:53.100
I need to find clues about where Reiji 
Akaba and the others are, too.

00:09:53.770 --> 00:09:54.620
My brother?

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:58.350
Wait! If you just rush out, 
we'll be separated aga—

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.580
Layra!

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:06.360
Darn it... What are we going to do?

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:12.340
I get it!

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:18.380
So a riding duel is when you ride a D-Wheel 
at high speeds to fight a duel.

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:19.230
It sounds fun!

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:24.010
Fun? We don't have time to participate 
in gambling duels!

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.210
But it's exciting, isn't it?

00:10:29.880 --> 00:10:33.720
Kurosaki! Kurosaki!

00:10:33.720 --> 00:10:36.230
It makes my entertainer's blood boil.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:40.180
I want to turn those cheers for 
Kurosaki into cheers for Dennis.

00:10:41.300 --> 00:10:42.990
Well said, Dennis!

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.660
I knew I didn't make a mistake with you!

00:10:48.630 --> 00:10:50.380
Okay, it's decided!

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:53.860
Let's give you a duel with Kurosaki.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:58.340
Kurosaki! Don't tell me you're going along with this!

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:03.320
If I get ten wins in this underground venue,

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.310
I'll be allowed to participate in the Friendship Cup!

00:11:06.790 --> 00:11:09.980
The Friendship Cup? What's that?

00:11:09.980 --> 00:11:12.320
City's greatest duel competition.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.040
Tops and Commons come together,

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:20.190
under the flag of harmony, to let their 
most valiant duelists take the stage.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:22.220
The event happens once per year!

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:24.300
And the winner gets...

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:31.240
The right to fight the King of Duelists, Jack Atlas!

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:35.440
The King of Duelists? So he's the strongest there is?

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:38.410
Is he the strongest, you ask? You bet he is!

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:42.650
Jack is the champion of City... 
No, of the whole world!

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.970
Then, it's decided, Gonny.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:45.680
What?

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:48.090
Well, if we take part in the Friendship Cup,

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:53.000
we'll meet lots of strong duelists, 
and ultimately get to fight the king.

00:11:53.000 --> 00:11:56.220
It's the perfect way to achieve the Lancers' objective.

00:11:56.220 --> 00:11:57.960
I am the one who will fight

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:00.130
the king.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.100
Will you? I don't think we'll know until we try.

00:12:07.070 --> 00:12:08.540
You two...

00:12:11.510 --> 00:12:13.150
Why is this happening?

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:19.550
For you all looking for a big payoff, I, 
the sharp-eyed promoter Gallagher,

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:22.520
am about to deliver a dream match!

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:26.120
Next, Kurosaki shoots for his tenth win.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:29.760
If he wins, he'll get to take 
part in the Friendship Cup!

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.510
But it won't be that easy.

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:35.930
The one who stands in his way is...

00:12:35.930 --> 00:12:39.080
The bold newcomer who caught my eye!

00:12:39.080 --> 00:12:44.040
His name... Dennis Mackfield!

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:47.690
Yes!

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.500
I'm an entertainer!

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:53.260
Let me bring you all into my fun show world!

00:12:53.260 --> 00:12:54.660
Let's enjoy...

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:56.680
show time!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:13:01.520
Now, the reigning champion, 
Kurosaki, takes the field!

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:05.820
Kurosaki! Kurosaki!

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:10.870
In accordance with underground duel 
rules, this will be a handicap match.

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:13.750
The newcomer, Dennis, will start 
with 4000 life points.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:17.010
And Kurosaki, with his nine straight wins...

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:22.780
will start with only 1000 points!

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:27.870
Even with a quarter of his opponent's life 
points, Kurosaki's still favored to win!

00:13:27.870 --> 00:13:32.890
But I, Gallagher, personally attest to Dennis's skill!

00:13:32.890 --> 00:13:36.230
If you want to make a lot of money, bet on Dennis.

00:13:36.560 --> 00:13:38.460
I'll bet on Dennis!

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:41.200
I bet everything on Kurosaki!

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:46.170
They're all blinded by greed...

00:13:46.170 --> 00:13:47.170
Outrageous!

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:52.240
I won't show mercy, just because I've got a handicap.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.450
I don't need it.

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:59.920
Let's go! I activate Field Spell Speed World Neo!

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:07.060
Duel Mode, on. Autopilot, stand by.

00:14:09.390 --> 00:14:11.460
Riding duel...

00:14:12.700 --> 00:14:14.200
Acceleration!

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:15.770
Duel!

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:18.030
I take the first move.

00:14:18.030 --> 00:14:21.370
I summon Raidraptor — Skull Eagle!

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:28.250
And I activate my spell card Raidraptor — Call!

00:14:28.650 --> 00:14:32.780
It lets me summon another monster, 
of the same name, from my deck.

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:38.150
I overlay my two Raidraptor — Skull Eagles!

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:42.090
Xyz Summon!

00:14:42.090 --> 00:14:47.100
Appear, Rank 3 Raidraptor — Fiend Eagle!

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:53.320
In that instant, the monster effect of the two 
Skull Eagles used as Xyz components

00:14:53.320 --> 00:14:57.670
increases Fiend Eagle's attack points by 300 each!

00:14:59.310 --> 00:15:02.960
And I activate the monster effect of Fiend Eagle!

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:04.750
I use one Overlay Unit

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:07.400
to deal damage to you, equal to the attack points

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.740
of one monster that was Special Summoned to the field!

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:16.090
All of a sudden...

00:15:16.400 --> 00:15:19.210
I set one card and end my turn.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:22.430
That's our reigning champion, Kurosaki!

00:15:22.430 --> 00:15:24.800
In just one turn, he's used Xyz Summon.

00:15:24.800 --> 00:15:29.040
And in a bold development, he's already 
done 1600 points of damage to Dennis!

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:32.380
Can he push him down all the way?

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:35.980
No way. The fun's only getting started.

00:15:37.270 --> 00:15:40.220
That's Yuya's line! Outrageous!

00:15:40.680 --> 00:15:42.690
My turn. Draw!

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:47.690
When there are monsters on my opponent's 
side of the field, but none on mine,

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:51.500
I can Special Summon Performage 
Wind Drainer from my hand.

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:57.100
When I succeed in Special Summoning 
it, its level decreases by 1.

00:15:57.360 --> 00:16:01.190
Then I summon Performage Ball 
Balancer from my hand.

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:07.190
I overlay Level 4 Wind Dancer and Ball Balancer!

00:16:11.300 --> 00:16:13.080
The show must go on!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:18.320
Sky magician, travel around the stage magnificently!

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.320
Xyz Summon!

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:25.700
Come out, Rank 4 Performage Trapeze Magician!

00:16:27.260 --> 00:16:29.230
He can use Xyz, too?

00:16:29.230 --> 00:16:31.200
Xyz versus Xyz?

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.940
I've never seen a fight like this before!

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:37.910
I use Fiend Eagle's other Overlay Unit 
to activate its monster effect!

00:16:38.230 --> 00:16:42.980
I deal damage to you, equal to the attack points 
of one Special Summoned monster.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:46.850
Take damage equal to Trapeze 
Magician's attack points!

00:16:46.850 --> 00:16:49.310
Now, this one's tough...

00:16:49.310 --> 00:16:54.030
Trapeze Magician's attack points 
are 2500. Dennis's life is 2400.

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.800
If this goes through...

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.600
Kurosaki's victory will be decided.

00:16:58.130 --> 00:17:00.650
I activate Trapeze Magician's effect.

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:03.830
I negate damage equal to, or less 
than, this card's attack points!

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:12.890
And I use one of Trapeze Magician's 
Overlay Units to let it attack twice.

00:17:13.950 --> 00:17:14.650
What?

00:17:14.650 --> 00:17:19.320
Battle, Trapeze Magician! Attack Fiend Eagle!

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.460
It's a total turnaround!

00:17:22.460 --> 00:17:25.020
Now it's Dennis who has Kurosaki 
backed against the wall!

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:27.800
Kurosaki's life points are down to 100!

00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:29.860
Is he finally going to lose?

00:17:29.860 --> 00:17:32.170
My next move is, of course, a direct attack.

00:17:32.170 --> 00:17:34.330
Get him, Trapeze Magician!

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:36.800
I activate my trap Necro Raptor!

00:17:36.800 --> 00:17:40.270
I reduce damage dealt by one direct attack to 0,

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:44.170
and Special Summon a Raidraptor 
from my graveyard.

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:48.300
I choose to return Raidraptor — Fiend Eagle!

00:17:52.720 --> 00:17:55.950
He's good with those trap cards. 
It's a little frustrating...

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.600
I set one card and end my turn.

00:17:59.690 --> 00:18:03.990
It's a tense match. They each have 
a blade at the other's throat...

00:18:04.280 --> 00:18:07.100
You can't take your eyes off it for a minute!

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:09.210
For Dennis to make it this far...

00:18:09.650 --> 00:18:11.970
That's LDS for you, I suppose.

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:15.340
LDS cultivates such practical dueling skills?

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.440
In that case... My turn!

00:18:18.760 --> 00:18:22.670
I activate Rank-Up-Magic Raid Force from my hand!

00:18:22.670 --> 00:18:26.220
I use Rank 3 Raidraptor — Fiend Eagle 
as a component,

00:18:26.220 --> 00:18:29.390
to Xyz Summon a Raidraptor that's one rank higher!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.420
Rank 4 Raidraptor — Force Strix!

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:37.070
Force Strix's effect.

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:43.080
I use one Overlay Unit to add Raidraptor — 
Necro Vulture from my deck to my hand,

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:44.410
and summon it!

00:18:45.900 --> 00:18:49.570
Then I tribute Necro Vulture to activate its effect!

00:18:49.570 --> 00:18:53.240
And I can add a Rank-Up-Magic from 
my graveyard to my hand!

00:18:53.240 --> 00:18:55.250
I add Rank-Up-Magic Raid Force.

00:18:55.720 --> 00:19:01.140
I use Force Strix as a component, to Xyz 
Summon a Raidraptor one rank higher!

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:06.720
Ferocious falcon, cut through fierce 
battles and flap your wings

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:08.660
to defeat your approaching enemies.

00:19:09.010 --> 00:19:12.870
Rank Up Xyz Change! Appear!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:17.580
Rank 5 Raidraptor — Blaze Falcon!

00:19:18.100 --> 00:19:20.250
Blaze Falcon's monster effect.

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:24.780
I can use one Overlay Unit to destroy 
your Special Summoned monsters,

00:19:24.780 --> 00:19:27.480
dealing 500 damage to you for each.

00:19:30.600 --> 00:19:31.900
Trapeze Magician!

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:34.460
And now, I'll cut you off completely.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:38.620
I activate my Equip Spell Raptor's Ultimate Mace!

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:43.220
I equip it to Blaze Falcon, to increase 
its attack points by 1000!

00:19:44.090 --> 00:19:47.570
Battle! Blaze Falcon, attack directly!

00:19:47.570 --> 00:19:49.560
Dennis has 1900 life points!

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.800
Will this be the end of his fight?

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:55.210
When a Special Summoned 
monster attacks directly,

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:59.510
Ball Balancer's effect activates from my graveyard, 
and Special Summons itself!

00:19:59.940 --> 00:20:01.400
It won't work.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:06.720
Blaze Falcon can attack directly, even if 
monsters are on your side of the field.

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.950
I activate my trap Pinch Breaker!

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.190
I change your monster's attack points

00:20:11.190 --> 00:20:13.880
to equal the defense points of one of my monsters.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:21.610
He took the hit!

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.830
But he managed to hang in there!

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:26.800
Blaze Falcon's effect.

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:32.460
When it deals damage to you, it can 
destroy one of your monsters.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:38.400
In that instant, Pinch Breaker's effect ends,

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.300
and Blaze Falcon's attack points return to normal.

00:20:42.320 --> 00:20:45.120
I set one card and end my turn.

00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:51.060
Damn you... Are you really from LDS?

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.760
That's right. Why do you ask?

00:20:55.730 --> 00:20:57.660
They've driven each other's life down to 100.

00:20:57.660 --> 00:21:00.200
There's no telling which will win!

00:21:00.530 --> 00:21:05.510
I don't know why you doubt my story, 
but let's make this even more exciting!

00:21:07.630 --> 00:21:10.230
Here it comes! My turn!

00:21:11.410 --> 00:21:15.040
I set the Pendulum Scale with Scale 2 
Performage Water Dancer

00:21:15.040 --> 00:21:19.160
and Scale 6 Performage Fire Dancer!

00:21:22.950 --> 00:21:27.350
Now, I can summon monsters between 
Levels 3 and 5 simultaneously!

00:21:28.300 --> 00:21:29.670
Pendulum Summon!

00:21:30.290 --> 00:21:33.040
Come to me, my monsters!

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:36.150
I summon two Performage Wing Sandwichmans

00:21:36.970 --> 00:21:39.940
and from my Extra Deck, Performage Ball Balancer!

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:44.750
Three monsters at once?

00:21:44.750 --> 00:21:47.650
And without tributing a monster of Level 5 or above?

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:52.910
The summoning method that's like magic 
would make any man lose his nerve.

00:21:52.910 --> 00:21:54.120
Its name...

00:21:59.040 --> 00:22:00.560
Pendulum Summon?

00:22:00.560 --> 00:22:03.800
Yes, in the underground duel venue, 
in City's central region.

00:22:03.800 --> 00:22:06.060
Send someone to monitor the situation at once.

00:22:06.060 --> 00:22:08.750
They may be hiding there.

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:09.750
I'll take care of it.

00:23:47.970 --> 00:23:52.620
Did you see? The summoning method that's like 
magic would make any man lose his nerve.

00:23:52.620 --> 00:23:56.750
Its name... Pendulum Summon!

00:23:57.660 --> 00:24:00.400
Will Kurosaki protect his #1 throne?

00:24:00.400 --> 00:24:03.320
Or will Dennis become the new #1?

00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:08.650
Kurosaki or Dennis? Dennis or Kurosaki?!

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:12.830
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Underground Riding Duel!!

00:24:12.830 --> 00:24:14.810
The fun is only getting started!
